<title>BULGARIA: Raiffeisenbank Bulgaria back in profit in 1996.</title>
<headline>Raiffeisenbank Bulgaria back in profit in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Raiffeisenbank Bulgaria posted 116.004 miliion levs net profit for last year after a 76.819 million lev loss for 1995, bank figures published in the State Gazette showed.</p>
<p>Raiffeisenbank Bulgaria was launched as a subsidiary of Raiffeisen Zentralbank Austria in 1994.</p>
<p>Figures from the bank's profit-and-loss account and balance sheet follow in million levs unless stated otherwise:</p>
<p>							1996	  1995</p>
<p> Total revenue				3,422.132    347.189</p>
<p> Net income on financial operations   1,447.479     59.916</p>
<p> Business and administration cost	 478.341    136.737</p>
<p> Provisions				     939.107	  0.0</p>
<p> Taxes						  224	  0.0</p>
<p> Profit					   116.004	  0.0</p>
<p> Loss						   0.0     76.819</p>
<p> Equity capital				 800.000    500.000</p>
<p> Reserves, including provisions	   939.107	  0.0</p>
<p> Total assets				19,997.992  1,765.594</p>
<p> Financial assets			  18,282.508  1,636.173</p>
<p> Cash					   2,171.627    237.190</p>
<p> Treasury portfolio			    83.800     13.600</p>
<p> Extended Interbank deposits	    9,485.045     70.290</p>
<p> Attracted interbank deposits	   1,088.248    383.958</p>
<p> Lending to non-financial clients     6,542.036  1,315.093</p>
<p> Capital including equity capital</p>
<p> and provisions			     1,739.107    383.996</p>
<p>* Items not included in the balance 36,932.557  1,524.689</p>
<p>* Under local accountancy standards items not included in the balance comprise guarantees and other commitments issued by the bank. -- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 911 88</p>
</text>
